Engine: an activation checked against the field the client saw (open fix 62).

STATUS: APPLIED 30 September 2026 by work order 197 (Part A.4, "open fix 26
... one more look") — orion2re 6f69de27 on orionlayer-local (before:
e4b2256a), this file's diff byte for byte (index lines included). Required
by tools/version_check.py since work order 197.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_activate_checked.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert 6f69de27` or
`patch -R -p1`, and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    MSG_ACTIVATE sets g_pending_field, and the NEXT fields::Get_Input_ takes
    it (fields.cpp) — whatever list that call belongs to. At a turn end the
    reports phase stands for 0.02-0.15 s with one whole-screen field and
    goes on by itself; an activation sent for it arrived after it had gone
    and SELECT NEW RESEARCH, built in between, took the index as its own
    field 1 when its input delay ran out (~1.4 s) and committed that
    research row. That is open fix 26, reproduced twice by work order 197
    (turn 9 and 11 of scratch SAVE4, nothing sent into the list).

    The client now sends the field's rect as ITS list shows it, after the
    index (int16 x, y, x_end, y_end — MSG_ACTIVATE's payload grows from 2
    to 10 bytes). Every Tick, which runs right before Get_Input_ takes a
    pending activation, compares that rect with the field at the index; if
    it differs the activation is dropped. An activation with no rect (an
    older client) is taken as before; an engine without this fix reads the
    first two bytes only, as before, so either side can be older.

    Written only in src/ext; nothing runs unless a client sends an
    activation, so an engine without OrionLayer behaves exactly as before.
    One marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 62.`, on one line at each changed
    place.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 864b6f0a..5d754c6a 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@ static bool Hide_Window_At_Start_() {
 std::atomic<bool> g_hide_window{Hide_Window_At_Start_()};
 int16_t g_pending_field = 0;
 int16_t g_activated_input = 0;
+// OrionLayer, open fix 62. The rect the client saw at the pending index (x, y, x_end, y_end), when it sent one.
+static bool g_pending_checked = false;
+static int16_t g_pending_rect[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};
 bool g_injected_mouse_pending = false;
 
 static Server g_server;
@@ -2030,6 +2033,11 @@ static void ProcessInput() {
             // overwritten by Interpret_Mouse_Input_() on normal clicks.
             if (cmd.param1 >= 0 && cmd.param1 < fields::_fields_count) {
                 g_pending_field = cmd.param1;
+                // OrionLayer, open fix 62. A client that names the field's rect gets it checked where the field is taken.
+                g_pending_checked = cmd.pairs.size() == 8;
+                if (g_pending_checked) {
+                    memcpy(g_pending_rect, cmd.pairs.data(), 8);
+                }
             }
             break;
 
@@ -2499,6 +2507,25 @@ void Tick(int16_t current_screen) {
     // Process queued input commands
     ProcessInput();
 
+    // OrionLayer, open fix 62. A pending activation is taken by the NEXT
+    // Get_Input_ (fields.cpp), which may belong to another list than the one
+    // the client answered: a screen that ended by itself in between (the
+    // reports phase's whole-screen field, gone in 0.02-0.15 s) handed its
+    // index to SELECT NEW RESEARCH, whose row 1 was then committed after its
+    // input delay (open fix 26). Every Tick runs right before that take, so
+    // an index that no longer names the field the client saw is dropped here.
+    if (g_pending_field > 0 && g_pending_checked) {
+        const bool same = g_pending_field < fields::_fields_count &&
+            fields::_fields[g_pending_field].x == g_pending_rect[0] &&
+            fields::_fields[g_pending_field].y == g_pending_rect[1] &&
+            fields::_fields[g_pending_field].x_end == g_pending_rect[2] &&
+            fields::_fields[g_pending_field].y_end == g_pending_rect[3];
+        if (!same) {
+            g_pending_field = 0;
+            g_pending_checked = false;
+        }
+    }
+
     // No clients? Skip serialization.
     if (g_server.ClientCount() == 0) return;
 
diff --git a/src/ext/ext_server.cpp b/src/ext/ext_server.cpp
index f31f2ac9..2a0ddde0 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_server.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_server.cpp
@@ -199,6 +199,10 @@ void Server::HandleClientMessage(Client& client) {
             InputCommand cmd{};
             cmd.type = MSG_ACTIVATE;
             memcpy(&cmd.param1, payload, 2);
+            // OrionLayer, open fix 62. Optional: int16 x, y, x_end, y_end of the field as the client saw it.
+            if (payload_len >= 10) {
+                cmd.pairs.assign(payload + 2, payload + 10);
+            }
             input_queue_.push_back(cmd);
         }
         break;
